# Cloudflare Containers' settings (`metacomputer vm create NAME --on cloudflare` writes them to config/vms/NAME.env), as
# comments: nothing here is read as a setting; config/defaults.env has the defaults every computer shares. Its docs:
# docs/cloudflare.md.
#   PLACE=cloudflare, PROVIDER=cloudflare, TRANSPORT=cloudflare
#   CLOUDFLARE_WORKER        its control Worker (metacomputer-NAME by default; vm create --worker), on workers.dev only;
#                            its Durable Object namespace, container application and registry repository are named
#                            after it. Fixed when it's made
#   SIZE                     standard-3 (the default: 2 vCPU, 8 GiB, 16 GB), standard-2 (1/6/12) or standard-4 (4/12/20)
#   IDLE_STOP                minutes after its last connection closes before its control Worker stops it (15 by
#                            default; 1 to 350: Cloudflare stops an idle container after 6 hours at most)
#   EGRESS                   internet or off: Cloudflare's outbound rules, outside the computer (net allow lists names)
# Its credentials, in the environment of vm create and vm delete only (from your secrets manager, for that command):
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN     an API token of the account (docs/cloudflare.md says which permissions)
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID    the account (32 hex digits)
# They reach lib/remote.py only. Everything else uses the computer's own key, made by vm create and kept beside its
# SSH keys ($SSH_DIR/cloudflare-key, 0600): lib/remote.py and the computer's broker (providers/cloudflare/broker.py) only.
